For the two that actually are adjectives (horned and barbed), that
does seem like the most plausible explanation. I'd instinctively
have assumed, however, that an ice devil _lived_ around ice and was
well adapted for dealing with it, rather than being made of it.
(Like a freshwater salmon, a mountain goat or a sea cow. Or, come to
think of it, a plains centaur or a hill orc.) So perhaps I would
expect an ice devil to be unlike most demons in being cold
resistant, but I wouldn't expect it to actually turn into water when
attacked with fire.

That does leave a bone devil as the one with the least obvious
meaning...
